  "note": "Exclusive display ownership. Totals count complete reservations, including unused capacity. The g3/g4/i5/dt3 used-byte fields are historical slice measurements, not current occupancy or available space. The 5120-byte widget strip can retain unfinished painting between physical grants. Glyph/raster/icon/copy-edge staging shares the 4096-byte transient scratch under physical access. GEM font staging writes complete pages within its 20480-byte reservation. The two font atlases are separate GEM and ATASCII assets. Shell backing retains 40960 bytes: its GUI owner is retired, but private text/fill entries and tests still use the fixed destination. Diagnostics borrow unassigned VRAM. The 4096-byte CPU aperture is a separate CPU address-space reservation, not a limit on VRAM workspace. See docs/history/vbxe-vram-audit.md for source consumers, gaps and reuse constraints. No reserved bank-zero growth. Mapped raster staging reserves 16384 bytes at $4C000; source and output share 1024-byte row slots under synchronous physical access, through the existing 4 KiB aperture."
